cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hydra: unified AMR, virulence, point-mutation, heteroresistance, MLST and lineage typing from bacterial assemblies and raw reads"
message: "If you use Hydra, please cite it and the reference databases it screened against (hydra db info NAME prints each one's citation)."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Hydra contributors"
    affiliation: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/iowa69/hydra"
url: "https://github.com/iowa69/hydra"
abstract: >-
  Hydra screens bacterial assemblies and raw reads for acquired resistance and
  virulence genes, organism-specific resistance point mutations, multi-locus
  sequence types and lineage typing schemes in a single pass over a single set
  of databases. From raw reads it additionally measures allele fractions at
  every catalogued mutation position, so heteroresistance - a resistance
  mutation carried by only some copies of a multi-copy locus, as in the 23S rRNA
  mutations behind linezolid resistance - is detected even though the assembly
  consensus is wild type.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - heteroresistance
  - MLST
  - bacterial genomics
  - virulence
  - linezolid
license: MIT
version: 1.4.0
date-released: "2026-08-08"
